==============================================================================

signal           marker             beta                  95% CI         p
excess_fixed     cal_sd         -0.00068   [-0.00114, -0.00021]    0.0041
excess_fixed     resp           -0.00105   [-0.00161, -0.00049]    0.0003
excess_fixed     hrv            -0.00045   [-0.00089, -0.00001]    0.0429
excess_adaptive  cal_sd         -0.00039   [-0.00091, +0.00012]    0.1359
excess_adaptive  resp           -0.00116   [-0.00175, -0.00057]    0.0001
excess_adaptive  hrv            -0.00014   [-0.00064, +0.00037]    0.5967

  A negative coefficient means a higher marker weakens the link
  between excess arousal and imminent failure, which is the same
  direction as the curve-shape moderation at trial level.

  per-subject slope against each marker (n = 16 subjects, one point each):
    cal_sd       r = -0.203 (p = 0.452)   rho = -0.265 (p = 0.322)
    resp         r = -0.087 (p = 0.750)   rho = -0.097 (p = 0.721)
    hrv          r = -0.078 (p = 0.773)   rho = +0.132 (p = 0.625)
  These are null. The mixed model uses every bin and models the
  clustering; the 16-point correlation discards that and is
  dominated by one extreme subject. Report both.

